                                                "sense_id": "58d5edc8-3820-310f-ac8a-922a2642da19",
                                                "text": "In particular, a very crisp quantifier such as “for all,” “there exists,” “at least 50 percent” tend to have less disperse weighting vectors while fuzzier quantifiers such as many tend to have a more disperse weighting vector."
